WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.167 --> 00:00:17.235
The next morning Miles was about to leave when Edward woke up.

2
00:00:17.255 --> 00:00:19.817
"Where are you going?"

3
00:00:20.417 --> 00:00:21.938
Edward said in a sleepy voice.

4
00:00:21.958 --> 00:00:24.700
"I'm freezing."

5
00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:30.324
"I'm just going out to run an errand," Miles replied.

6
00:00:31.532 --> 00:00:33.833
"You'll be warmer if you pull the covers over your head."

7
00:00:36.034 --> 00:00:40.896
Too tired to order Miles to do that for him, Edward just grunted and tugged on the covers.

8
00:00:42.997 --> 00:00:46.798
Half an hour later, Miles returned with some secondhand clothes for Edward.

9
00:00:49.299 --> 00:00:52.281
Made of cheap material, they clearly showed signs of wear.

10
00:00:52.301 --> 00:00:59.744
"At least they're clean and warm, and I can mend the smaller holes," Miles thought.

11
00:01:01.368 --> 00:01:02.589
"I hope they're the right size."

12
00:01:04.651 --> 00:01:08.234
Miles held up a shirt and compared it to the lump in the bed across the room.

13
00:01:10.616 --> 00:01:12.437
He sat down and took out a needle and thread.

14
00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:20.063
It took him five tries, but at last he succeeded in threading the needle.

15
00:01:22.325 --> 00:01:25.027
Miles hummed quietly while he worked on his mending.

16
00:01:26.909 --> 00:01:29.011
"Ouch! That's a sharp needle!"

17
00:01:29.451 --> 00:01:30.332
Miles said aloud.

18
00:01:31.724 --> 00:01:34.205
He sucked his finger as he looked over at the bed.

19
00:01:36.106 --> 00:01:37.126
Edward did not stir.

20
00:01:37.146 --> 00:01:41.948
"Poor lad must be exhausted," he thought.

21
00:01:41.968 --> 00:01:46.710
"I'll have to wake him soon, so we can eat and be on our way to Hendon Hall."

22
00:01:48.711 --> 00:01:52.713
Miles wished he had more money, so that he could afford better clothes for Edward.

23
00:01:54.294 --> 00:01:55.314
But these would have to do.

24
00:01:56.715 --> 00:01:59.596
He still needed to pay for their food and lodging along the way.

25
00:02:01.032 --> 00:02:03.473
Finished with the mending, Miles called Edward.

26
00:02:03.493 --> 00:02:06.734
"Time to get up, Your Majesty!"

27
00:02:08.234 --> 00:02:11.535
There was still no sign of life from the lump in the bed.

28
00:02:13.096 --> 00:02:15.737
Miles finally approached the bed and threw back the covers.

29
00:02:16.837 --> 00:02:19.218
"Edward?" The boy was gone!

30
00:02:21.858 --> 00:02:23.719
Miles looked around the small room.

31
00:02:25.019 --> 00:02:26.760
There was no place for Edward to hide.

32
00:02:29.204 --> 00:02:31.185
Just then someone knocked at the door.

33
00:02:32.766 --> 00:02:37.167
Miles opened it, expecting Edward, but a servant pushed past him with breakfast.

34
00:02:38.668 --> 00:02:39.508
"Not so fast!"

35
00:02:39.969 --> 00:02:40.609
Miles said.

36
00:02:40.629 --> 00:02:43.230
"Have you seen the boy who was with me?"

37
00:02:45.271 --> 00:02:47.232
The servant laid the dishes on the table.

38
00:02:47.252 --> 00:02:50.573
"Um—" "Where is he?"

39
00:02:50.953 --> 00:02:51.814
Miles demanded.

40
00:02:51.834 --> 00:02:57.176
"Soon after you left, a young man came to the inn."

41
00:02:58.572 --> 00:03:00.533
The servant anxiously wrung his hands.

42
00:03:00.553 --> 00:03:06.337
"He said that you wanted the boy to meet you in the woods beyond the bridge.

43
00:03:08.079 --> 00:03:09.800
So I brought the young man to your room.

44
00:03:11.521 --> 00:03:13.802
He woke up the lad and delivered his message."

45
00:03:13.823 --> 00:03:17.785
"And what did the boy say to that?

46
00:03:18.806 --> 00:03:20.407
I can't imagine he was very happy."

47
00:03:20.427 --> 00:03:27.452
"Well, he did grumble about being disturbed 'so early,' as he put it.

48
00:03:29.624 --> 00:03:31.685
But he left with the young man right away.

49
00:03:34.007 --> 00:03:39.289
On the way out, he remarked that you showed bad manners in sending a stranger instead of coming

50
00:03:39.329 --> 00:03:43.252
yourself." "I didn't send a stranger, you fool!"

51
00:03:44.792 --> 00:03:46.313
Miles began to pace the room.

52
00:03:47.534 --> 00:03:49.215
"Perhaps no harm will come to the boy.

53
00:03:50.215 --> 00:03:51.856
I'll eat and then I'll go in search of him.

54
00:03:52.977 --> 00:03:54.098
Quick! Set the table.

55
00:03:55.458 --> 00:03:55.959
No, wait!"

56
00:03:56.859 --> 00:03:58.080
Miles stopped pacing.

57
00:03:59.672 --> 00:04:02.313
"Someone tried to make it look like the boy was still in bed.

58
00:04:02.793 --> 00:04:10.895
Why?" "I don't know for sure," the servant said, "but I saw the young man fooling with the

59
00:04:10.935 --> 00:04:15.096
covers." "It's clear that someone wanted to deceive me."

60
00:04:16.997 --> 00:04:18.937
Miles smacked his forehead with his hand.

61
00:04:18.957 --> 00:04:22.978
"Whoever it was wanted to gain time so they could escape.

62
00:04:24.179 --> 00:04:25.299
Was the young man alone?"

63
00:04:25.319 --> 00:04:28.220
"Yes, all alone."

64
00:04:30.232 --> 00:04:30.812
"Are you sure?"

65
00:04:31.213 --> 00:04:32.173
Miles persisted.

66
00:04:32.193 --> 00:04:33.914
"Think hard."

67
00:04:35.575 --> 00:04:38.416
The servant wrinkled his brow as if that would help him think.

68
00:04:39.577 --> 00:04:40.958
"Oh! Now I remember!

69
00:04:41.998 --> 00:04:43.799
No one came here with the young man.

70
00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:49.342
But I happened to be looking out the window when he and the boy reached the bridge."

71
00:04:50.903 --> 00:04:51.664
"What happened then?"

72
00:04:52.184 --> 00:04:53.685
Miles thundered impatiently.

73
00:04:53.705 --> 00:04:58.147
"Just then the innkeeper called me—" "No, no!

74
00:04:58.407 --> 00:04:59.528
What happened to the boy?"

75
00:05:01.388 --> 00:05:05.229
"A man dressed in rags stepped out of the shadows and followed them."

76
00:05:05.249 --> 00:05:07.530
"Did you get a good look at him?"

77
00:05:07.550 --> 00:05:12.872
"His arm was in a sling, and he had a patch over one eye."

78
00:05:15.872 --> 00:05:18.073
Miles sat down at the table and rubbed his eyes.

79
00:05:18.093 --> 00:05:22.074
"I can't believe I've lost my poor little friend.

80
00:05:22.094 --> 00:05:27.136
I promised myself I'd take care of him until he was well."

81
00:05:29.772 --> 00:05:30.512
"Don't worry.

82
00:05:30.572 --> 00:05:31.813
I'm sure you'll find him.

83
00:05:33.453 --> 00:05:36.394
And one more thing," the servant said as he opened the door.

84
00:05:36.414 --> 00:05:39.475
"That fellow with the eye patch?

85
00:05:40.475 --> 00:05:42.876
He limped slightly and walked with a cane."

86
00:05:45.017 --> 00:05:45.877
"Oh no!"

87
00:05:47.017 --> 00:05:47.977
Miles groaned.

88
00:05:47.998 --> 00:05:53.719
"That man is probably the same brute who claimed that Edward was his son!"

89
00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:56.000
Miles stood up.

90
00:05:57.556 --> 00:06:00.744
He hated to leave his food, but he had to find Edward at once.

91
00:06:02.768 --> 00:06:03.931
The boy could be in trouble!
